 "case:locations.building.art.props.8.label": "To the towpath",
 "case:locations.building.description": "The common parts of the building: a front hall with post boxes and a buzzer panel, the main stairs, and at the back a bike store with its own door onto the canal towpath. Flat 1, Owen’s, opens off the front hall.",
 "case:locations.building.hotspots.hs_bd_bikestore.label": "Bike store",
 "case:locations.building.hotspots.hs_bd_bikestore.text": "Bikes, scooters, a pram. The door at the far end opens straight onto the canal towpath, on the same keypad codes as the front door. From here the back stairs go up to Flats 2, 3 and 4. Anyone who came in this way would never pass through the front hall.",
 "case:locations.building.hotspots.hs_bd_boat.label": "Narrowboat",
 "case:locations.building.hotspots.hs_bd_boat.text": "Now you know Marcus wasn’t running, you go back to the towpath. The narrowboat moored behind the bike store has a chimney, a cat and a man on deck with a roll-up, who has seen everything that happens here for six years.",
 "case:locations.building.hotspots.hs_bd_flat1.label": "Flat 1",
 "case:locations.building.hotspots.hs_bd_flat1.text": "Owen’s door, with a small camera above it. It looks out across the front hall to the main entrance and the foot of the main stairs. It can’t see the bike store, or the back stairs. Flat 1, on the ground floor, also has a back door of its own straight onto the towpath.",
 "case:locations.building.hotspots.hs_bd_notice.label": "Notice board",
 "case:locations.building.hotspots.hs_bd_notice.text": "Bin days, a lost cat, and a laminated notice: ‘Door system queries — please contact the residents’ committee: Owen Hart, Flat 1.’",
 "case:locations.building.hotspots.hs_bd_panel.label": "Entry panel",
 "case:locations.building.hotspots.hs_bd_panel.text": "A keypad and intercom by the main entrance. Residents and their guests use the same codes for the front door, the bike store door and their own flats. Visitors buzz up; a flat can let them in from a phone.",
 "case:locations.building.hotspots.hs_bd_sacks.label": "Stairs cupboard",
 "case:locations.building.hotspots.hs_bd_sacks.text": "A cupboard under the main stairs, its padlock hanging open. Owen keeps his stock in here.",
 "case:locations.building.hotspots.hs_bd_towpath.label": "The towpath",
 "case:locations.building.hotspots.hs_bd_towpath.text": "Outside the bike store door, on the back wall of the building two floors up, is Flat 3’s bathroom vent. A neighbour on a narrowboat laughs: ‘When he’s in the shower it steams like a kettle. You can set your watch by it — every night before he films.’",
 "case:locations.building.name": "The Ropeworks",
 "case:locations.building.summary": "The front hall, the stairs and the bike store.",
 "case:locations.doyles.art.props.0.label": "Front door",
 "case:locations.doyles.art.props.1.label": "Hall",
 "case:locations.doyles.art.props.2.label": "Coat cupboard",
 "case:locations.doyles.art.props.3.label": "Desk",
 "case:locations.doyles.art.props.4.label": "Kitchen",
 "case:locations.doyles.art.props.5.label": "Cupboards",
 "case:locations.doyles.art.props.6.label": "Fridge",
 "case:locations.doyles.art.props.7.label": "Island",
 "case:locations.doyles.art.props.8.label": "Back door",
 "case:locations.doyles.description": "A Victorian terrace on the edge of Victoria Park: school bags in the hall, running shoes by the door, the calendar on the fridge crammed with clubs and lessons. Hannah, on compassionate leave, has asked you in. Marcus is out; the children are at school.",
 "case:locations.doyles.hotspots.hs_dh_coats.label": "Coat cupboard",
 "case:locations.doyles.hotspots.hs_dh_coats.text": "Coats, scooters, a box of hats. And on the top shelf, a shoebox labelled in marker.",
 "case:locations.doyles.hotspots.hs_dh_cupboard.label": "Cupboard above the kettle",
 "case:locations.doyles.hotspots.hs_dh_cupboard.text": "Alfie’s medicines live in the cupboard above the kettle, out of his reach. Hannah takes down a pharmacy box.",
 "case:locations.doyles.hotspots.hs_dh_desk.label": "Hannah’s desk",
 "case:locations.doyles.hotspots.hs_dh_desk.text": "A laptop on a pile of marking, a webcam, a whiteboard of fractions. Hannah opens her tutoring account to show you her week.",
 "case:locations.doyles.hotspots.hs_dh_doorbell.label": "Video doorbell",
 "case:locations.doyles.hotspots.hs_dh_doorbell.text": "A video doorbell by the front door. Hannah hesitates, then opens its app on her phone and finds Thursday evening.",
 "case:locations.doyles.hotspots.hs_dh_fridge.label": "Fridge",
 "case:locations.doyles.hotspots.hs_dh_fridge.text": "The family calendar, Alfie’s allergy plan, and a dosing chart for his immunotherapy, one tick for every morning. On Thursday 7 March someone has written ‘J’s video 9pm!’ and drawn a little camera.",
 "case:locations.doyles.hotspots.hs_dh_ipad.label": "iPad on the counter",
 "case:locations.doyles.hotspots.hs_dh_ipad.text": "The family iPad, propped against the fruit bowl, open at the family group chat. Hannah scrolls back to Thursday for you without being asked.",
 "case:locations.doyles.hotspots.hs_dh_sharps.label": "Under the sink",
 "case:locations.doyles.hotspots.hs_dh_sharps.text": "Under the kitchen sink: bleach, bin bags, and a yellow sharps bin with a sealed lid and a slot, for Alfie’s used pens. When it’s full it goes back to the pharmacy to be burned, unopened.",
 "case:locations.doyles.hotspots.hs_dh_shoes.label": "Running shoes",
 "case:locations.doyles.hotspots.hs_dh_shoes.text": "Two pairs of running shoes by the door, a man’s size twelve and a girl’s size five spikes, and above them a black running jacket with ‘DT’ in reflective letters across the back. On the wall, a row of medals: ‘Evie Doyle — County Cross-Country, U17, 1st’.",
 "case:locations.doyles.lockedHint": "Hannah would have to invite you.",
 "case:locations.doyles.name": "The Doyles’ House",
 "case:locations.doyles.summary": "Hannah and Marcus’s home, by Victoria Park.",
 "case:locations.flat.art.props.0.label": "Window — canal",
 "case:locations.flat.art.props.1.label": "Kitchen counter",
 "case:locations.flat.art.props.10.label": "Front door",
 "case:locations.flat.art.props.2.label": "Studio",
 "case:locations.flat.art.props.3.label": "Bathroom",
 "case:locations.flat.art.props.4.label": "Kitchen island",
 "case:locations.flat.art.props.5.label": "Ring light",
 "case:locations.flat.art.props.6.label": "Rug",
 "case:locations.flat.art.props.7.label": "Sofa",
 "case:locations.flat.art.props.8.label": "Hallway",
 "case:locations.flat.art.props.9.label": "Coat hooks",
 "case:locations.flat.description": "Flat 3, The Ropeworks: an old rope factory by the canal, turned into four flats. One long room — kitchen at one end, sofa at the other, a ring light still standing by the island. The front door hangs crooked where the police forced it.",
 "case:locations.flat.hotspots.hs_fl_bag.label": "The takeaway bag",
 "case:locations.flat.hotspots.hs_fl_bag.text": "Thambi’s brown paper bag, still folded on the island beside the empty rice tub. The police took the curry and left the bag.",
 "case:locations.flat.hotspots.hs_fl_bathroom.label": "Bathroom",
 "case:locations.flat.hotspots.hs_fl_bathroom.text": "A small bathroom with a big shower. The extractor fan vents straight out through the back wall of the building, onto the canal towpath below.",
 "case:locations.flat.hotspots.hs_fl_drawer.label": "Kitchen drawer",
 "case:locations.flat.hotspots.hs_fl_drawer.text": "The drawer everyone has: takeaway menus, batteries, a broken corkscrew. And a pharmacy bag.",
 "case:locations.flat.hotspots.hs_fl_floor.label": "Under the island",
 "case:locations.flat.hotspots.hs_fl_floor.text": "Somebody stood at this island and doctored the curry. You get down on the floor with a torch and run it along the kickboard.",
 "case:locations.flat.hotspots.hs_fl_fridge.label": "Fridge door",
 "case:locations.flat.hotspots.hs_fl_fridge.text": "An allergy action plan with Jonah’s photo on it. Beside it, a child’s felt-tip drawing of two stick figures in capes: ‘ME AND UNCLE JONAH — SUPERHEROES.’",
 "case:locations.flat.hotspots.hs_fl_hooks.label": "Coat hooks",
 "case:locations.flat.hotspots.hs_fl_hooks.text": "Jonah’s black crossbody bag hangs on the hook nearest the door. Inside, a small zip pouch, open and empty. Lena says his pens lived in there, and nowhere else.",
 "case:locations.flat.hotspots.hs_fl_keypad.label": "Door keypad",
 "case:locations.flat.hotspots.hs_fl_keypad.text": "A smart lock with a keypad, the frame around it splintered. Lena opens the lock’s app on her phone and shows you Thursday’s history.",
 "case:locations.flat.hotspots.hs_fl_ringlight.label": "Ring light",
 "case:locations.flat.hotspots.hs_fl_ringlight.text": "The ring light and camera, still aimed at the island. The memory card is gone — the police took it. Whatever he filmed at 21:29, his followers saw it before they did.",
 "case:locations.flat.hotspots.hs_fl_rug.label": "The rug",
 "case:locations.flat.hotspots.hs_fl_rug.text": "Where the paramedics worked on him: tape, wrappers, a blood-pressure cuff’s packaging — and two clear plastic tubes.",
 "case:locations.flat.hotspots.hs_fl_window.label": "Window",
 "case:locations.flat.hotspots.hs_fl_window.text": "Below the window, the canal and the towpath — joggers, cyclists, narrowboats. At night it’s dark down there, and nobody looks up.",
 "case:locations.flat.name": "Jonah’s Flat",
 "case:locations.flat.summary": "Where Jonah died. Kitchen and living room.",
 "case:locations.studio.art.props.0.label": "Window",
 "case:locations.studio.art.props.1.label": "Desk",
 "case:locations.studio.art.props.2.label": "Chair",
 "case:locations.studio.art.props.3.label": "Shelf",
 "case:locations.studio.art.props.4.label": "Whiteboard",
 "case:locations.studio.art.props.5.label": "PR boxes",
 "case:locations.studio.art.props.6.label": "Rug",
 "case:locations.studio.description": "The second bedroom, which Jonah turned into an office: two monitors, a good microphone, soundproofing foam on the walls. PR boxes from brands are stacked to the ceiling. It smells of new cardboard.",
 "case:locations.studio.hotspots.hs_st_boxes.label": "PR boxes",
 "case:locations.studio.hotspots.hs_st_boxes.text": "Free gifts from brands hoping for a mention: hot sauces, knives, a pizza oven. Every label reads ‘Jonah Pryce, c/o Doyle Talent’ — every parcel went through Marcus first.",
 "case:locations.studio.hotspots.hs_st_drawer.label": "Desk drawer",
 "case:locations.studio.hotspots.hs_st_drawer.text": "Chargers, lens caps, two passports — and a folder of household papers: the mortgage, the boiler, the insurance.",
 "case:locations.studio.hotspots.hs_st_laptop.label": "Laptop",
 "case:locations.studio.hotspots.hs_st_laptop.text": "Jonah’s laptop, asleep on the desk. Wake it and it asks for a six-digit passcode.",
 "case:locations.studio.hotspots.hs_st_messages.label": "Laptop: messages",
 "case:locations.studio.hotspots.hs_st_messages.text": "His messages sync from his phone. The last conversation he had with anyone who wasn’t a follower is with his manager.",
 "case:locations.studio.hotspots.hs_st_receipts.label": "Laptop: RECEIPTS",
 "case:locations.studio.hotspots.hs_st_receipts.text": "With Lena’s passcode the laptop opens on the last thing Jonah worked on: a script, and a folder of screenshots.",
 "case:locations.studio.hotspots.hs_st_shelf.label": "Shelf",
 "case:locations.studio.hotspots.hs_st_shelf.text": "A glass award — ‘Food Creator of the Year 2023’ — and a framed photo of Jonah and a small boy in matching capes, both giving the camera a thumbs-up.",
 "case:locations.studio.hotspots.hs_st_whiteboard.label": "Whiteboard",
 "case:locations.studio.hotspots.hs_st_whiteboard.text": "His content calendar for March. Thursday 7: ‘THAMBI RD 2 — 9pm’. Monday 11, ringed three times in red: ‘09:00 — RECEIPTS — no going back’.",
 "case:locations.studio.name": "Jonah’s Studio",
 "case:locations.studio.summary": "His office and edit suite.",
 "case:locations.thambi.art.props.0.label": "Tables",
 "case:locations.thambi.art.props.1.label": "Front door",
 "case:locations.thambi.art.props.2.label": "The pass",
 "case:locations.thambi.art.props.3.label": "Stoves",
 "case:locations.thambi.art.props.4.label": "Dry store",
 "case:locations.thambi.art.props.5.label": "Packing station",
 "case:locations.thambi.description": "Eleven tables and an open kitchen behind a long pass, shut since Friday. Someone has sprayed MURDERER across the shutter. Inside it still smells of curry leaves and coconut.",
 "case:locations.thambi.hotspots.hs_th_camera.label": "Kitchen camera",
 "case:locations.thambi.hotspots.hs_th_camera.text": "A camera over the pass, installed for the insurers. Priya has had Thursday night copied for her solicitors.",
 "case:locations.thambi.hotspots.hs_th_packing.label": "Packing station",
 "case:locations.thambi.hotspots.hs_th_packing.text": "Paper bags, tubs, and a roll of round orange stickers printed with Thambi’s elephant. You peel one off and try to lift it again: it tears the paper unless you’re very slow and very careful.",
 "case:locations.thambi.hotspots.hs_th_pot.label": "Stock pot",
 "case:locations.thambi.hotspots.hs_th_pot.text": "The big pot the curry came out of, scrubbed and empty now. A police evidence tag on the handle: ‘Sampled 08/03 — see lab report CU-0308’.",
 "case:locations.thambi.hotspots.hs_th_sign.label": "Sign by the pass",
 "case:locations.thambi.hotspots.hs_th_sign.text": "Hand-painted, nine years old: ‘NUT-FREE KITCHEN SINCE 2015 — ask us anything.’ Someone has drawn a skull on it in marker, through the window.",
 "case:locations.thambi.hotspots.hs_th_store.label": "Dry store",
 "case:locations.thambi.hotspots.hs_th_store.text": "Sacks of rice and lentils, tins of coconut milk, a wall of spices in labelled jars. Right at the back, behind the rice, a jar that doesn’t match the others.",
 "case:locations.thambi.hotspots.hs_th_tablet.label": "Order tablet",
 "case:locations.thambi.hotspots.hs_th_tablet.text": "The tablet at the pass that takes delivery orders. Priya brings up order #4471: the order, the allergy note, and the courier’s photo when he left it.",
 "case:locations.thambi.name": "Thambi",
 "case:locations.thambi.summary": "Priya’s restaurant in Dalston, shut by the council.",
 "case:setting": "Hackney · East London · March 2024",
 "case:sketchCredit": "SKETCH: SITE VISIT, 11 MARCH 2024 · NOT TO SCALE",
 "case:sketchTitle": "HACKNEY",
 "case:stayLabel": "Stay in Hackney",
 "case:tagline": "A food critic with a deadly allergy, a one-star review, and a takeaway that killed him.",
 "case:timeline.conclusion": "At 21:17 Jonah was alive and the bag was sealed. At 21:19, while he showered, someone opened his door with the guest code; by 21:24 the curry was poisoned and his pens were useless. Whoever did it had made very sure to be seen somewhere else.",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_999.text": "Jonah calls 999: the pens aren’t working",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_999.time": "21:33",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_delivered.teaser": "How the curry reached the door.",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_delivered.text": "Mihai leaves the sealed bag at Jonah’s door",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_delivered.time": "21:04",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_entry.teaser": "What the front door remembers.",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_entry.text": "Someone opens Flat 3 with the guest code",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_entry.time": "21:19",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_evie.teaser": "A message sent that evening.",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_evie.text": "Evie posts ‘DONE YOUR RUN DAD’ in the family chat",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_evie.time": "21:41",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_home.teaser": "When the last person came home.",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_home.text": "Marcus gets home alone, from the canal end of the street",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_lena.teaser": "Someone was in the building who said they weren’t.",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_lena.text": "Lena goes into Owen’s flat",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_out.teaser": "Who went out that evening.",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_out.text": "Marcus leaves home in his running gear",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_packed.teaser": "What happened to the curry before it left the restaurant.",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_packed.text": "Priya seals Jonah’s order at Thambi",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_packed.time": "20:47",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_spiked.teaser": "When the curry was poisoned.",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_spiked.text": "The curry is spiked",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_story.text": "Jonah posts a story: the bag still sealed, a shower first",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_story.time": "21:17",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_tasting.text": "Jonah posts himself taking the first spoonful",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_tasting.time": "21:29",
 "case:timeline.prompt": "Put Thursday night’s events in the order they really happened. Times you know for certain are shown; reason out the rest.",
 "case:timeline.title": "Thursday night, reconstructed",
 "case:title": "Last Order",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_hannah_close.insight": "Marcus and Jonah were at war in their last week. Hannah overheard their row on Sunday and has been protecting her husband.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_hannah_close.response.0": "…I didn’t know about these. ‘Think of Hannah and the kids’? What does that mean?",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_hannah_close.response.1": "All right. On Sunday the third, at lunch, they went out into the garden. I heard Jonah say, ‘You’ve been using my name.’ Then Marcus came in white as a sheet, and Jonah left without his pudding.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_hannah_close.response.2": "Marcus told me it was a contract dispute. I wanted to believe him.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_hannah_close.title": "They weren’t getting on",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_lena_pilates.insight": "Lena didn’t walk home at ten to ten. She let herself into the building at 21:02 and spent the evening in Owen’s flat downstairs.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_lena_pilates.response.0": "…Yes. I left the class early. I came back at about nine, but I didn’t go up. I went to Owen’s flat. We’ve been… since Christmas.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_lena_pilates.response.1": "I was there when the sirens started. I ran upstairs and they were already working on him, and I said ‘pilates’ because it was the first word that came out.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_lena_pilates.response.2": "I didn’t go near our flat. Ask Owen. His camera sees his door.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_lena_pilates.title": "Lena was in the building",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_marcus_home.insight": "Marcus left the house with Evie at 20:55 and came back alone at 21:49, from the canal end of the street. He now says he went for a walk.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_marcus_home.response.0": "…All right. I walked. Round the park, along the canal. I needed to think. Jonah was about to wreck everything I’d built — my business, my house, my family.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_marcus_home.response.1": "So yes, I walked by the water for an hour feeling sorry for myself. I never went near The Ropeworks.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_marcus_home.title": "Marcus went out",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_marcus_inbox.insight": "The business inbox was Marcus’s, and Marcus was asking restaurants for money through it. He calls it normal business.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_marcus_inbox.response.0": "…Fine. I ran it. Mostly. Somebody had to.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_marcus_inbox.response.1": "And yes, I asked restaurants for collab fees. Everyone in this industry does. Some paid, some didn’t. That’s not a crime, it’s a rate card.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_marcus_inbox.response.2": "It isn’t murder, either.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_marcus_inbox.title": "Marcus ran the inbox",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_marcus_run.insight": "Evie ran Marcus’s 7.2 km wearing his watch and carrying his phone. Marcus admits it now — and says he spent the evening in his garden office.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_marcus_run.response.0": "…Fine. Evie took my watch and phone on her run. My knee’s been bad, and I didn’t want to break the streak. Five hundred and twelve days. Vanity, I know.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_marcus_run.response.1": "I didn’t mention it because it’s embarrassing, not because it’s sinister. I was in my garden office all evening, doing contracts.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_marcus_run.title": "Marcus didn’t run",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_marcus_thambi.insight": "Marcus suggested the Thambi video himself, and told Jonah to order ‘around nine’. He chose the restaurant and the time.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_marcus_thambi.response.0": "So I suggested it. It’s my job to suggest content. A second-chance video was always going to do numbers.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_marcus_thambi.response.1": "‘Around nine’ because nine is when people are on their phones. That’s not a plot. That’s an algorithm.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_marcus_thambi.title": "The Thambi video was Marcus’s idea",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_marcus_walk.insight": "Marcus was seen keying in at the bike store at 21:18, and Jonah’s new pens — the ones that should have saved him — ended up in the Doyles’ own sharps bin.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_marcus_walk.response.0": "…",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_marcus_walk.response.1": "You tell him what the man on the narrowboat saw, and where Jonah’s pens were found: on top of his son’s used needles, in his own kitchen. He looks at you for a long time. When he speaks, it isn’t to you. It is to ask for a solicitor.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_marcus_walk.title": "Marcus was at The Ropeworks",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_mihai_account.insight": "The account belongs to someone else. Mihai rents it, as thousands of couriers do — which is why he has kept away from the police. He saw a woman going into Flat 1 as he came in.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_mihai_account.response.0": "…Please. Andrei is my cousin’s friend. He has the papers, I have the bicycle. I pay him a hundred pounds a week to use his account. If the police find out, I lose everything.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_mihai_account.response.1": "But I told you the truth about the bag. The sticker was perfect.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_mihai_account.response.2": "And one more thing. When I came in, a blonde woman with a yoga mat was at the door downstairs, Flat 1. A man opened it and she went in. She looked at me like I was not there.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_mihai_account.title": "Mihai rides on a borrowed account",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_owen_alone.insight": "Lena was in Owen’s flat from 21:03 until the commotion upstairs. His door camera shows her going in, and shows nobody else in the front hall but the courier.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_owen_alone.response.0": "…Right. Yeah. She was here. I didn’t say because, well. Her fiancé had just died upstairs.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_owen_alone.response.1": "I’ll do better than my word, though. My door camera sees my door and the front hall. Here — every minute of Thursday night.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_owen_alone.response.2": "He scrolls back through the camera app on his phone and hands it to you.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_owen_alone.title": "Owen wasn’t alone",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_priya_contact.insight": "Three days before the review, Jonah’s business inbox asked Thambi for a £1,500 ‘collab fee’. Priya refused, and the one-star video followed.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_priya_contact.response.0": "Yes. All right. They wanted fifteen hundred pounds to be nice to me. I told them where to go.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_priya_contact.response.1": "Three days later, the video. I never told the police. How would it sound? ‘He tried to shake me down, I said no, and then he died eating my food.’",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_priya_contact.response.2": "I thought it was him. Jonah. Was it not?",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_priya_contact.title": "Thambi was asked to pay",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_priya_nut_free.insight": "Since February Priya has cooked with a chilli crisp that ‘may contain peanuts’, and she hid the jar. She is terrified the death really was her fault.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_priya_nut_free.response.0": "…Where did you find that?",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_priya_nut_free.response.1": "My supplier ran out of my usual chilli oil in February. That one tasted right. I saw ‘may contain’ and told myself it was just lawyers covering themselves. When I heard how he died, I hid it at the back of the store.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_priya_nut_free.response.2": "I didn’t put it in his curry. It goes in the devilled dishes, never the curry. But I’ve been lying awake asking myself if a spoon went in the wrong pot.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_priya_nut_free.title": "Thambi wasn’t quite nut-free",
 "deductions:deductions.d_hannah.conclusion": "From 21:00 to 21:45 Hannah was on video with a ten-year-old, teaching fractions, and the session was recorded. Whoever let themselves into Flat 3 at 21:19, it wasn’t her.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_hannah.options.0": "No — she was tutoring on camera from 21:00 to 21:45",
 "deductions:deductions.d_hannah.options.1": "Yes — her lesson finished early, at 21:15",
 "deductions:deductions.d_hannah.options.2": "Yes — she left a photo in front of her camera and slipped out",
 "deductions:deductions.d_hannah.proofLabels.0": "Where Hannah was",
 "deductions:deductions.d_hannah.proofLabels.1": "When the door opened",
 "deductions:deductions.d_hannah.question": "Could Hannah have opened Jonah’s door at 21:19?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_hannah.title": "Hannah was on camera",
 "deductions:deductions.d_lena.conclusion": "At 21:19, when the guest code opened Flat 3, Lena was walking across the back of Owen’s online class with a glass of water. At 21:24 she was still on his sofa. Whoever was upstairs, it wasn’t her.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_lena.options.0": "Yes — she left Owen’s flat by his towpath door at 21:15",
 "deductions:deductions.d_lena.options.1": "Yes — Owen’s class was pre-recorded, not live",
 "deductions:deductions.d_lena.options.2": "No — she is on camera in Owen’s flat at 21:19 and 21:24",
 "deductions:deductions.d_lena.proofLabels.0": "Where Lena was",
 "deductions:deductions.d_lena.proofLabels.1": "When the door opened",
 "deductions:deductions.d_lena.question": "Could Lena have opened Jonah’s door at 21:19?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_lena.title": "Lena was on camera",
 "deductions:deductions.d_pens.conclusion": "Jonah collected two new 0.3 mg pens on 26 February. The pens he used were 0.15 mg — half the dose — and eighteen months out of date, with their labels peeled off. Somebody swapped them.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_pens.options.0": "Someone swapped his new pens for old, weaker ones",
 "deductions:deductions.d_pens.options.1": "He’d left his new pens at the gym and grabbed old ones",
 "deductions:deductions.d_pens.options.2": "He injected too late, after he’d already collapsed",
 "deductions:deductions.d_pens.options.3": "His new pens came from a faulty batch",
 "deductions:deductions.d_pens.proofLabels.0": "The pens by his body",
 "deductions:deductions.d_pens.proofLabels.1": "The pens he should have had",
 "deductions:deductions.d_pens.question": "Why didn’t Jonah’s adrenaline pens save him?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_pens.title": "The wrong pens",
 "deductions:deductions.d_run.conclusion": "Thursday’s run was faster than Marcus’s best ever, at a cadence he has never run at, with a heart rate fifteen beats above the highest he has ever recorded — a teenage runner’s numbers. Evie ran it for him: ‘DONE YOUR RUN DAD’. Marcus has no alibi.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_run.options.0": "Yes — his watch tracked every step",
 "deductions:deductions.d_run.options.1": "No — he faked the route with a GPS app",
 "deductions:deductions.d_run.options.2": "Yes, but he cut the route short and sat on a bench",
 "deductions:deductions.d_run.options.3": "No — Evie ran it, wearing his watch",
 "deductions:deductions.d_run.proofLabels.0": "Thursday’s run",
 "deductions:deductions.d_run.proofLabels.1": "Who was wearing the watch",
 "deductions:deductions.d_run.question": "Was Marcus really running round Victoria Park on Thursday night?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_run.title": "Somebody else’s run",
 "deductions:deductions.d_shakedown.conclusion": "Through Jonah’s business inbox, restaurants were asked for ‘collab fees’, and those who refused got a savaging. Jonah found out who was behind it, and was going to name them on Monday at nine and then go to the police.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_shakedown.options.0": "That he was leaving Lena for someone else",
 "deductions:deductions.d_shakedown.options.1": "That restaurants were being shaken down for money in his name",
 "deductions:deductions.d_shakedown.options.2": "That Thambi had made other customers ill before",
 "deductions:deductions.d_shakedown.options.3": "That he was quitting reviews to open his own restaurant",
 "deductions:deductions.d_shakedown.proofLabels.0": "Jonah’s plan",
 "deductions:deductions.d_shakedown.proofLabels.1": "Proof of the demands",
 "deductions:deductions.d_shakedown.question": "What was Jonah going to reveal on Monday?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_shakedown.title": "The shakedown",
 "deductions:deductions.d_source.conclusion": "The torn foil corner under the island comes from a 300 mg sachet of peanut protein — Alfie Doyle’s immunotherapy, made to be opened and stirred into food. The killer brought it from the Doyles’ house.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_source.options.0": "Owen’s peanut flour, carried up the back stairs",
 "deductions:deductions.d_source.options.1": "Thambi’s chilli crisp, spooned in at packing",
 "deductions:deductions.d_source.options.2": "A sachet of Alfie’s peanut immunotherapy",
 "deductions:deductions.d_source.options.3": "A Hart Fuel protein ball, crumbled over the top",
 "deductions:deductions.d_source.proofLabels.0": "What the killer left behind",
 "deductions:deductions.d_source.proofLabels.1": "Whose medicine it was",
 "deductions:deductions.d_source.question": "Where did the peanut powder come from?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_source.title": "Alfie’s medicine",
 "deductions:deductions.d_spiked.conclusion": "The peanut was dry powder, only in the curry from the top of the tub — none further down, none in Thambi’s pot, and no oil, so it wasn’t the chilli crisp. And the bag reached Jonah’s door sealed. Somebody opened it inside the flat and sprinkled the powder on.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_spiked.options.0": "Cross-contamination from a ladle in Thambi’s kitchen",
 "deductions:deductions.d_spiked.options.1": "Thambi’s chilli crisp, sprinkled on at packing",
 "deductions:deductions.d_spiked.options.2": "Someone sprinkled it on after the curry was delivered",
 "deductions:deductions.d_spiked.options.3": "The courier opened the bag on the stairs and added it",
 "deductions:deductions.d_spiked.proofLabels.0": "Signs of tampering",
 "deductions:deductions.d_spiked.proofLabels.1": "The bag was sealed when it arrived",
 "deductions:deductions.d_spiked.question": "How did peanut get into Jonah’s curry?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_spiked.title": "Spiked after delivery",
 "deductions:deductions.d_towpath.conclusion": "A very tall man in a black running jacket with reflective letters — D-something — keyed in at the bike store at 21:18 and walked back towards Victoria Park five minutes later. Marcus, six foot four, with no alibi, came home from the canal end at 21:49.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_towpath.options.0": "Owen, slipping round from his own back door",
 "deductions:deductions.d_towpath.options.1": "Lena, out of Owen’s flat by the towpath",
 "deductions:deductions.d_towpath.options.2": "Marcus, in his reflective running jacket",
 "deductions:deductions.d_towpath.options.3": "The courier, coming back for a tip",
 "deductions:deductions.d_towpath.proofLabels.0": "Who was seen at the bike store",
 "deductions:deductions.d_towpath.proofLabels.1": "Where Marcus really was",
 "deductions:deductions.d_towpath.question": "Who let themselves in by the bike store at 21:18?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_towpath.title": "The man on the towpath",
 "deductions:deductions.d_window.conclusion": "At 21:17 Jonah said he was going for a shower, and the pipes ran from about 21:18. At 21:18 someone came in by the back with Flat 3’s guest code; at 21:19 the same code opened his door, and at 21:24 someone let themselves out from inside. Five minutes, while the water ran.",
 "deductions:deductions.d_window.options.0": "Between 21:04 and 21:16, while he set up his ring light",
 "deductions:deductions.d_window.options.1": "Between 21:29 and 21:33, while he was filming",
 "deductions:deductions.d_window.options.2": "Before 21:04, on the stairs, in the courier’s two minutes",
 "deductions:deductions.d_window.options.3": "Between 21:19 and 21:24, while Jonah was in the shower",
 "deductions:deductions.d_window.proofLabels.0": "The door opened",
 "deductions:deductions.d_window.proofLabels.1": "Jonah was in the shower",
 "deductions:deductions.d_window.question": "When could someone have spiked the curry?",
 "deductions:deductions.d_window.title": "Five minutes in the shower",
 "dialogues:statements.st_hannah_babysit.text": "Lena does Alfie’s breakfast and sachet every Wednesday, and has had our key for years.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_hannah_close.text": "Marcus and Jonah got on like brothers. Never a cross word.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_hannah_oit.text": "Alfie’s immunotherapy is a 300 mg sachet of peanut protein a day, torn open and stirred into his yoghurt.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_hannah_out.text": "Marcus went out in his running things at about 20:55, while I set up my lesson.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_hannah_row.text": "At Sunday lunch I heard Jonah tell Marcus, ‘You’ve been using my name.’ They didn’t speak again that day.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_hannah_tutoring.text": "From 21:00 to 21:45 I was tutoring online, camera on, the whole time.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_lena_codes.text": "The guest code is for family and team: Hannah and Marcus both have it. It opens the building doors too, front and back.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_lena_inbox.text": "Marcus has run Jonah’s business inbox for two years. Jonah never touched his messages.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_lena_new_pens.text": "Jonah collected two new pens on 26 February and kept them in the pouch in his crossbody bag.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_lena_owen.text": "I left pilates early. From 21:03 to 21:47 I was in Owen’s flat downstairs. We’ve been seeing each other.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_lena_pilates.text": "I was at pilates until 21:30, walked home slowly and came up the stairs at 21:50.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_lena_policy.text": "Our joint life policy pays £450,000 to whichever of us is left. It’s for the mortgage.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_lena_shower.text": "Jonah always set up his camera, then showered before he filmed. Anyone who watched his videos knew it.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_marcus_content.text": "I suggested the Thambi video, and that he order around nine. Suggesting content is my job.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_marcus_fees.text": "I ran Jonah’s inbox, and I asked restaurants for ‘collab fees’. Everyone in this industry does.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_marcus_home.text": "Evie took my watch and phone on her run, to keep my streak going. I was in my garden office all evening.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_marcus_inbox.text": "Half the team used Jonah’s inbox — assistants, interns, Lena. I couldn’t tell you who sent what.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_marcus_run.text": "From 21:00 until about 21:30 I was running round Victoria Park. It’s on my running app.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_marcus_thambi.text": "The Thambi second-chance video was Jonah’s idea, not mine.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_marcus_walk.text": "I went for a walk along the canal to think. I never went near The Ropeworks.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_mihai_andrei.text": "I am Andrei P. It is my account.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_mihai_sealed.text": "At 21:04 I left the bag on Flat 3’s mat with the sticker unbroken, took the photo and went.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_mihai_yoga.text": "Coming in at 21:03 I saw a blonde woman with a yoga mat go into Flat 1, on the ground floor.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_owen_alone.text": "I was on my own in my flat all evening, teaching a class online.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_owen_flour.text": "The peanut flour is for my protein balls. Jonah slated them in a video.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_owen_lena.text": "Lena was with me in my flat from 21:03 until 21:47, when we heard the commotion and she ran upstairs.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_owen_pipes.text": "Jonah’s shower pipes thumped through my wall from about 21:18, for five minutes or so.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_priya_alibi.text": "I was at my pass from 20:30 until I closed. My kitchen camera shows every minute.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_priya_chili.text": "Since February I’ve used a chilli crisp labelled ‘may contain peanuts’. I hid it because I was terrified it was my fault.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_priya_fee.text": "On 2 January Jonah’s business inbox asked me for a £1,500 ‘collab fee’. I said no, and three days later came the review.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_priya_no_contact.text": "Before his review, nobody from Jonah’s side ever contacted me.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_priya_nut_free.text": "Nothing in my kitchen contains nuts. Nothing, in nine years.",
 "dialogues:statements.st_priya_sealed.text": "I packed Jonah’s order myself and sealed the bag with our sticker at 20:47.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hannah_alfie.lines.0": "My son Alfie. He’s eight — it runs in the family. Since September he’s been on oral immunotherapy: a tiny dose of peanut protein every day, to train his body not to panic.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hannah_alfie.lines.1": "It’s a powder in a little foil sachet. You tear it open and stir it into his yoghurt at breakfast. Three hundred milligrams. It’s done wonders for him. In the wrong person it could kill.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hannah_alfie.lines.2": "Lena does his breakfast and his sachet on Wednesdays, when I’m in early for staff training. She’s had a key to our house for years.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hannah_alfie.prompt": "Does anyone else in the family have Jonah’s allergy?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hannah_evening.lines.0": "What were you doing on Thursday evening, Mrs Doyle?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hannah_evening.lines.1": "Working. I tutor online three nights a week — Thursday was a Year 6 boy, fractions, from nine until quarter to ten, camera on the whole time. Alfie was asleep upstairs.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hannah_evening.lines.2": "Marcus went out for his run at about five to nine, while I was setting up my lesson. He never misses a day.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hannah_evening.prompt": "What were you doing on Thursday evening?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hannah_family.lines.0": "Like brothers. Honestly. Marcus found him, built him, stood by him through every pile-on. There was never a cross word between them.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hannah_family.lines.1": "Whatever you’re thinking, you can stop thinking it.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hannah_family.prompt": "How did Marcus and Jonah get on?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hannah_jonah.lines.0": "Loud. Vain. Generous to a fault. When Alfie was diagnosed, Jonah sat with him in hospital and told him they were ‘the peanut club’ and the club was very exclusive.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hannah_jonah.lines.1": "The internet thought he was cruel. He was cruel on camera. Off it, he was my little brother.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hannah_jonah.prompt": "What was Jonah like, as a brother?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hannah_pens.lines.0": "We do — Alfie’s, my son. His in-date pens are in his school bag and by his bed, always two of each.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hannah_pens.lines.1": "And I keep his old ones for training — the junior dose, 0.15 milligrams, all expired — so I can show babysitters and the school what to do. A box in the coat cupboard.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hannah_pens.lines.2": "You think someone used Alfie’s pens? Come to the house. I’ll show you myself.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hannah_pens.lines.3": "The Doyles’ House is now open to you.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hannah_pens.prompt": "Who keeps old adrenaline pens?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hannah_sunday.lines.0": "I don’t know. Truly. That was Sunday the third — the last time we were all together. Marcus said it was business — a brand deal, a contract. He’s been sleeping badly ever since.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hannah_sunday.lines.1": "We remortgaged the house to start the agency. If Jonah had walked, we’d have lost it. Is that what you want me to say?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_hannah_sunday.prompt": "What were they rowing about on Sunday?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_lena_codes.lines.0": "The door has a keypad. Jonah and I had our own codes. The cleaner has one that only works on Monday and Thursday mornings.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_lena_codes.lines.1": "And there’s the guest code, for family and team. Hannah has it, Marcus has it — he’s always dropping off PR boxes. It works on the building doors too, front and back.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_lena_codes.prompt": "Who could get into the flat?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_lena_evening.lines.0": "Where were you on Thursday evening?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_lena_evening.lines.1": "Pilates. The studio on Wallis Road, the half-eight class. I left the flat at twenty past eight. Jonah was ordering his curry for the video — he was so pleased with himself.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_lena_evening.lines.2": "The class finished at half nine. I walked home slowly, and when I came up the stairs at ten to ten there were paramedics in our flat. That’s all.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_lena_evening.prompt": "Where were you on Thursday evening?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_lena_inbox.lines.0": "Marcus. For two years. Jonah never touched his DMs — there were thousands a day. Brand deals, collabs, all of it went through Marcus.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_lena_inbox.lines.1": "Why? What did you find?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_lena_inbox.prompt": "Who ran Jonah’s business inbox?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_lena_laptop.lines.0": "So it wasn’t an accident. Someone did this to him. The police didn’t even want his laptop — they took his phone and that was it.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_lena_laptop.lines.1": "The password’s our anniversary. One, four, zero, six, one, nine. It’s on the desk in the studio. Everything syncs to it, even his messages.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_lena_laptop.prompt": "May I look at Jonah’s laptop?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_lena_owen.lines.0": "Since Christmas. Jonah was never home, and when he was, he was filming. Owen was downstairs. That’s the whole sordid story.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_lena_owen.lines.1": "I was forty feet away while he died, and I didn’t hear a thing. I’ll live with that.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_lena_owen.prompt": "How long have you and Owen been…?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_lena_pens.lines.0": "He never went anywhere without two. They lived in a little zip pouch in his crossbody bag — the black one on the hook by the door.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_lena_pens.lines.1": "And they weren’t old. He collected new ones from the chemist on the twenty-sixth of February. I went with him. The police keep saying ‘expired’, and it makes no sense.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_lena_pens.prompt": "Tell me about Jonah’s adrenaline pens.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_lena_policy.lines.0": "We took it out when we bought the flat — the mortgage adviser talked us into it. Four hundred and fifty thousand to whoever’s left. It pays off the mortgage, and then some.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_lena_policy.lines.1": "I know exactly how that looks, with everything else. I didn’t kill him for a flat.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_lena_policy.prompt": "Tell me about the life policy.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_lena_routine.lines.0": "Always the same. Order, set up the ring light and the camera at the island, then shower — he would not go on camera with flat hair, not ever. Then plate up and film.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_lena_routine.lines.1": "Anyone who’s watched more than three of his videos could tell you that. He even joked about it.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_lena_routine.prompt": "How did Jonah film his reviews?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_marcus_evening.lines.0": "Where were you on Thursday night, Mr Doyle?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_marcus_evening.lines.1": "Running. Round Victoria Park, from nine until about half past. Five hundred and twelve days in a row — I don’t miss, even with a dodgy knee.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_marcus_evening.lines.2": "Don’t take my word for it. It’s all on the app, to the second. Here.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_marcus_evening.lines.3": "He holds up his phone, his running profile open.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_marcus_evening.prompt": "Where were you on Thursday night?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_marcus_inbox.lines.0": "The inbox? Half the team used it — assistants, interns, Lena, whoever was free. Thousands of messages a day. I couldn’t tell you who sent what.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_marcus_inbox.lines.1": "Restaurants pay for features all the time. It’s how the industry works. If someone got creative with the wording, that’s not on me.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_marcus_inbox.prompt": "Who ran Jonah’s business inbox?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_marcus_jonah.lines.0": "I found him when he had nine thousand followers and a phone propped against a ketchup bottle. Seven years. I made him a brand. He made me a living. That’s management.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_marcus_jonah.lines.1": "And he was my wife’s little brother. My kids’ favourite uncle. Whatever you’ve heard, we were family.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_marcus_jonah.prompt": "Tell me about you and Jonah.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_marcus_thambi.lines.0": "Jonah’s, all his. He couldn’t resist a fight. I’d have told him to leave it — you don’t go back to a place you’ve buried.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_marcus_thambi.lines.1": "But that was Jonah. Once he’d decided, nobody could stop him.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_marcus_thambi.prompt": "Whose idea was the Thambi video?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_mihai_delivery.lines.0": "Tell me about Thursday’s delivery to The Ropeworks.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_mihai_delivery.lines.1": "I am Andrei. Andrei P., it is my account. I picked up from Thambi at ten to nine, I rode to Hackney Wick. Somebody buzzed me in from the phone.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_mihai_delivery.lines.2": "I go up to Flat 3, I put the bag on the mat, I take the photo — the app wants a photo. The sticker was on it, perfect. Then I go. One minute, maybe two.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_mihai_delivery.prompt": "Tell me about the delivery.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_mihai_police.lines.0": "I’m not avoiding. I am working. The police call the number on the account, and the account is… complicated.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_mihai_police.lines.1": "I did nothing to that bag. I swear on my mother.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_mihai_police.prompt": "Why have you been avoiding the police?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_mihai_work.lines.0": "Two years. Twelve hours a day, six days. In the rain you get more money, so I like the rain.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_mihai_work.lines.1": "The app gives me two minutes for the stairs. If I’m late, my rating drops. If my rating drops, I don’t eat.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_mihai_work.prompt": "How long have you been delivering?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_owen_class.lines.0": "The class? Sure — I record every one for my subscribers. Thursday, nine o’clock, Core and Mobility. Thirty minutes of me telling people to breathe.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_owen_class.lines.1": "Lena’s in the background, mind. Probably why I didn’t offer it.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_owen_class.prompt": "May I see the recording of your class?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_owen_evening.lines.0": "Where were you on Thursday evening?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_owen_evening.lines.1": "In my flat, on my own, all night. I taught a live class online at nine — core and mobility, thirty minutes — then I had a shower and watched the football.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_owen_evening.lines.2": "First I knew of anything was the sirens.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_owen_evening.prompt": "Where were you on Thursday evening?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_owen_hartfuel.lines.0": "Peanut flour, for my protein balls. Hart Fuel. Fifteen hundred subscribers, all handmade in my kitchen.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_owen_hartfuel.lines.1": "Yeah, I know how that looks. Jonah did a video on them — said they tasted like a gym bag. Sales went up, funnily enough. I wasn’t going to kill a bloke for free advertising.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_owen_hartfuel.prompt": "What’s in the sacks by your door?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_owen_logs.lines.0": "Me, actually. I look after the door system for the landlord — I’ve got the admin login. Every code, every buzz.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_owen_logs.lines.1": "Here, I’ll pull up Thursday. Knock yourself out.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_owen_logs.prompt": "Who can see the building’s door records?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_owen_pipes.lines.0": "The pipes. This building’s an old rope factory — when Jonah runs his shower, the pipes in my wall thump like someone’s in there with a hammer.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_owen_pipes.lines.1": "They went from about eighteen minutes past nine, for five minutes or so. I remember because I was teaching my class and had to talk over them.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_owen_pipes.prompt": "Did you hear anything from upstairs?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_priya_jonah.lines.0": "I thought he was a bully with a ring light. I still do. And I’m sorry he’s dead. Both things.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_priya_jonah.lines.1": "People like him think a restaurant is a set for their videos. It’s a family’s whole life.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_priya_jonah.prompt": "What did you think of Jonah?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_priya_kitchen.lines.0": "Ms Ratnam, tell me about your kitchen.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_priya_kitchen.lines.1": "Nine years, and not one peanut through my door. No cashews, no almonds, no satay — nothing. My nephew nearly died from a sesame bun when he was six. I know what an allergy looks like.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_priya_kitchen.lines.2": "I cooked that curry myself, from the pot I’d fed three other people from that night. I packed it, I folded the bag and I sealed it with our sticker at quarter to nine. Nothing in my kitchen contains nuts. Nothing.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_priya_kitchen.prompt": "Tell me about your kitchen.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_priya_lab.lines.0": "My solicitor got the report on Saturday. They found peanut in the curry. Of course they did — that’s why I’m under investigation.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_priya_lab.lines.1": "They say a garnish of mine must have been contaminated. I don’t garnish that curry. Read it properly — read where the peanut was.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_priya_lab.lines.2": "She pushes a printed report across the table to you.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_priya_lab.prompt": "What did the police lab find?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_priya_review.lines.0": "He came in January, ate for twenty minutes, and called us ‘a lawsuit with a menu’. Two million people watched it. Our bookings halved in a week.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_priya_review.lines.1": "I’d never heard of him before that video. Nobody from his side ever contacted me — not a message, not a call. He just turned up and destroyed us.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_priya_review.lines.2": "So I told him to order again. Publicly. I wanted him to eat my food and admit he was wrong. Now look.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_priya_review.prompt": "What happened with Jonah’s review?",
 "dialogues:topics.t_priya_thursday.lines.0": "Where I am every night: at the pass, from half eight until I’d cleaned down. My kitchen camera shows every minute of it. The police have the footage. They just don’t care.",
 "dialogues:topics.t_priya_thursday.prompt": "Where were you on Thursday night?",
 "evidence:evidence.adult_pens.detail": "Under the Doyles’ kitchen sink, the yellow sharps bin where they put Alfie’s used pens and needles, to go back to the pharmacy for burning. Through its slot, on top of everything else: two adrenaline pens, 0.3 mg, adult dose. Pharmacy label: ‘Mr J. PRYCE’. EXP 09/2025.\n\nUnused.",
 "evidence:evidence.adult_pens.name": "Pens in the sharps bin",
 "evidence:evidence.adult_pens.summary": "Jonah’s two new adult pens, unused, dropped into the Doyles’ sharps bin.",
 "evidence:evidence.boater_statement.detail": "Ray Okafor lives on the narrowboat Second Wind, moored on the towpath behind The Ropeworks:\n\n‘About quarter past nine I was on deck having a smoke. A very tall bloke in a black running jacket — hood up, reflective letters across the back, D-something — came along from the Victoria Park end and stood under the building like he was waiting for a bus. Then he keyed himself in at the bike store door.\n\nFive minutes later he came out and went back the way he came. Walking fast, not running. I thought: odd sort of run, that.’",
 "evidence:evidence.boater_statement.name": "The narrowboat owner",
 "evidence:evidence.boater_statement.summary": "21:18: a very tall man in a black running jacket keyed in at the bike store.",
 "evidence:evidence.building_log.detail": "The Ropeworks — door access log, Thursday 7 March:\n\n18:11 Main entrance — code: Flat 3 JONAH\n20:23 Main entrance — exit button\n21:02 Main entrance — code: Flat 3 LENA\n21:03 Main entrance — opened remotely from Flat 3 (intercom app)\n21:18 Bike store (towpath door) — code: Flat 3 GUEST\n21:25 Bike store (towpath door) — exit button\n21:44 Main entrance — emergency services override",
 "evidence:evidence.building_log.name": "Building door log",
 "evidence:evidence.building_log.summary": "21:18: someone came in the back way, by the bike store, with Flat 3’s guest code.",
 "evidence:evidence.chili_oil.detail": "At the back of Thambi’s dry store, behind the sacks of rice: a jar of ‘Golden Lotus chilli crisp’, two-thirds used. Written on the lid in marker: ‘OPENED 12/2 — P.’\n\nThe small print on the label: ‘May contain peanuts.’\n\nIt is an oily paste of fried chilli, garlic and shallot.",
 "evidence:evidence.chili_oil.name": "Jar of chilli crisp",
 "evidence:evidence.chili_oil.summary": "Hidden in Thambi’s dry store: ‘May contain peanuts.’",
 "evidence:evidence.delivery_photo.detail": "Delivery app, order #4471 — delivered 21:04, left at door (contactless).\n\nPhoto: a brown paper bag on the doormat of Flat 3, the round orange Thambi sticker across its fold, unbroken.\n\nCourier: ‘Andrei P.’ ★4.9 — 2,311 deliveries. Profile photo: a heavy-set man in his forties with a grey beard.",
 "evidence:evidence.delivery_photo.name": "Proof-of-delivery photo",
 "evidence:evidence.delivery_photo.summary": "21:04: the bag at Jonah’s door, seal unbroken. Courier: ‘Andrei P.’",
 "evidence:evidence.dm_thambi.detail": "One of the 31 screenshots in the RECEIPTS folder. Jonah’s business inbox, 2 January 2024, to Thambi:\n\n‘Hi Priya! Jonah’s been eyeing up Thambi 🔥 For a feature we ask a small collab fee (£1,500). Otherwise he’ll be visiting as a regular customer — and he’s very honest 😉 Let me know! Team J’\n\nThambi’s reply: ‘We don’t pay for reviews. Come and eat like anyone else.’\n\nThe one-star video went up on 5 January.",
 "evidence:evidence.dm_thambi.name": "Screenshot: message to Thambi",
 "evidence:evidence.dm_thambi.summary": "2 January: ‘a small collab fee (£1,500)… otherwise he’ll be visiting as a regular customer’.",
 "evidence:evidence.doyle_doorbell.detail": "The Doyles’ video doorbell, Thursday 7 March:\n\n20:55 — Marcus and Evie leave together in running gear. Evie has a watch on each wrist: her own small one, and a big black one.\n21:43 — Evie comes back alone, flushed, out of breath.\n21:49 — Marcus comes back alone, walking fast from the canal end of the street, hood up.",
 "evidence:evidence.doyle_doorbell.name": "The Doyles’ doorbell camera",
 "evidence:evidence.doyle_doorbell.summary": "20:55 out together; 21:43 Evie back; 21:49 Marcus back, from the canal end.",
 "evidence:evidence.family_chat.detail": "The family group chat, open on the iPad on the Doyles’ kitchen counter. Thursday 7 March:\n\n21:41 Evie: DONE YOUR RUN DAD 🏃‍♀️ 7.2k in 35 mins!!! you owe me £20 💸\n21:42 Hannah: Shh, tutoring! x\n21:58 Marcus: Legend. Knee’s grateful x",
 "evidence:evidence.family_chat.name": "The Doyle family chat",
 "evidence:evidence.family_chat.summary": "21:41, Evie: ‘DONE YOUR RUN DAD… you owe me £20’.",
 "evidence:evidence.jonah_messages.detail": "On Jonah’s laptop, synced from his phone.\n\nTuesday 5 March, 22:14\nMarcus: Mate. Don’t do this. Let me explain. Think of Hannah and the kids.\nJonah: You should have thought of them. Monday.\n\nWednesday 6 March, 11:02\nMarcus: Fine. At least do the Thambi second-chance video tomorrow night. It’ll do numbers either way. Order around nine.\nJonah: Fine. Last thing I do for you.",
 "evidence:evidence.jonah_messages.name": "Messages: Jonah and Marcus",
 "evidence:evidence.jonah_messages.summary": "‘Think of Hannah and the kids.’ ‘Monday.’ And: ‘order around nine’.",
 "evidence:evidence.jonah_stories.detail": "Saved and reposted by thousands of his followers.\n\n21:17 — The Thambi bag on his kitchen island, its round orange sticker unbroken across the fold. Caption: ‘Round two with Thambi 🙏 They swear they’re nut-free. Shower first, then we find out 😅’\n\n21:29 — Jonah at the island under his ring light, hair still wet. He rips the bag open down its side — ‘Never break the seal, it’s bad luck’ — spoons half the curry onto a plate and leaves the rest in the tub. ‘Moment of truth…’ He takes the first spoonful and gives the camera a thumbs-up.",
 "evidence:evidence.jonah_stories.name": "Jonah’s last stories",
 "evidence:evidence.jonah_stories.summary": "21:17, the bag still sealed: ‘Shower first.’ 21:29, he tears it open and takes the first spoonful.",
 "evidence:evidence.lab_report.detail": "Public analyst’s report for the Metropolitan Police, samples from the deceased’s flat, 8 March 2024.\n\nCurry on the plate: peanut protein at a very high level. Under the microscope the surface carries a fine, pale powder. No fragments of chilli, garlic or shallot; no added oil.\nCurry left at the bottom of the tub: no peanut detected.\nCoconut rice: no peanut detected.\nThambi’s stock pot (sampled 8 March): no peanut detected.",
 "evidence:evidence.lab_report.name": "Food lab report",
 "evidence:evidence.lab_report.summary": "Peanut in the curry on his plate, as a fine powder on top. None in what was left in the tub.",
 "evidence:evidence.life_policy.detail": "In the studio desk drawer, the schedule of a life insurance policy taken out last spring, when Jonah and Lena bought the flat:\n\n‘Joint life, first death. Lives assured: Mr Jonah Pryce, Ms Lena Novak. Sum assured: £450,000, payable to the surviving life assured.’\n\nWith Jonah dead, it pays Lena £450,000.",
 "evidence:evidence.life_policy.name": "Joint life policy",
 "evidence:evidence.life_policy.summary": "£450,000 to whichever of Jonah and Lena outlives the other.",
 "evidence:evidence.marcus_history.detail": "Marcus’s running app is logged in on the family iPad, too. His runs this month, apart from Thursday:\n\n6–8 km each, pace 5:35–5:50/km. Heart rate average 148–155, max 171–176. Cadence 162–166.\n\nBest pace he has ever recorded: 4:58/km. Highest heart rate ever: 179.",
 "evidence:evidence.marcus_history.name": "Marcus’s month of runs",
 "evidence:evidence.marcus_history.summary": "Every other run: slower, with a lower heart rate and a different cadence.",
 "evidence:evidence.marcus_running.detail": "Marcus’s public profile: ‘MarcusD 🚣 — Streak: 512 days’.\n\nThursday 7 March, 20:58–21:33 — ‘Evening run, round Victoria Park’, 7.2 km. Pace 4:51/km. Heart rate average 165, max 194. Cadence 178 steps/min.",
 "evidence:evidence.marcus_running.name": "Marcus’s running app",
 "evidence:evidence.marcus_running.summary": "Thursday, 20:58–21:33: 7.2 km round Victoria Park, logged on his watch.",
 "evidence:evidence.medicine_box.detail": "In the cupboard above the Doyles’ kettle, a pharmacy box: ‘ALFIE DOYLE — Peanut protein oral immunotherapy, 300 mg sachets. ONE sachet daily: open and mix into yoghurt.’ Dispensed 1 March: 30 sachets.\n\nThe dosing chart on the fridge is ticked for every day from 1 to 11 March. Eleven used. There should be nineteen left.\n\nThere are eighteen.",
 "evidence:evidence.medicine_box.name": "Alfie’s medicine box",
 "evidence:evidence.medicine_box.summary": "Peanut protein, 300 mg sachets. One sachet is unaccounted for.",
 "evidence:evidence.old_pens_box.detail": "A shoebox on the top shelf of the Doyles’ coat cupboard, labelled in marker ‘OLD PENS — TRAINING ONLY — DO NOT USE’. Hannah uses expired pens to show babysitters and school staff what to do.\n\nInside: two junior pens, 0.15 mg, EXP 08/2022, pharmacy labels ‘ALFIE DOYLE’. The list taped inside the lid says four.",
 "evidence:evidence.old_pens_box.name": "Box of old pens",
 "evidence:evidence.old_pens_box.summary": "‘OLD PENS — TRAINING ONLY.’ The lid says four. There are two.",
 "evidence:evidence.owen_camera.detail": "Flat 1 door camera — it sees Owen’s door and the front hall, but not the back stairs. Thursday 7 March:\n\n21:02 — Lena, with a yoga mat, knocks at Flat 1.\n21:03 — Owen lets her in, as a courier with a paper bag passes behind her and goes up the main stairs.\n21:05 — The courier comes back down, empty-handed, and leaves.\n21:44 — Paramedics and two police officers run in and up the stairs.\n21:47 — Lena comes out of Flat 1 and runs upstairs.\n\nNo other movement in the front hall from 20:30 to 22:00.",
 "evidence:evidence.owen_camera.name": "Owen’s door camera",
 "evidence:evidence.owen_camera.summary": "Lena in Flat 1 from 21:03 to 21:47. Nobody else in the front hall but the courier.",
 "evidence:evidence.owen_class.detail": "Owen’s live online class, ‘Core & Mobility’, Thursday 7 March, 21:00–21:30, recorded for his subscribers. Owen faces the camera in his living room; behind him, a sofa and the kitchen.\n\n21:19 — Lena walks behind him with a glass of water and sits on the sofa.\n21:24 — Still on the sofa, scrolling her phone. Owen, mid-plank: ‘And that’s my neighbour’s shower, folks — the pipes in this building, honestly.’\n21:30 — Class ends. Lena is still there.",
 "evidence:evidence.owen_class.name": "Recording of Owen’s class",
 "evidence:evidence.owen_class.summary": "21:19, Lena crosses the room behind Owen; at 21:24 she’s on his sofa.",
 "evidence:evidence.owen_flour.detail": "In the cupboard under the main stairs, which Owen rents from the building as a store: three 5 kg sacks of fine, pale peanut flour, one opened and clipped shut, and flat-pack boxes printed ‘HART FUEL — handmade peanut protein balls’.\n\nA sticky note on the inside of the door, in capitals: ‘OWEN — PLEASE keep this locked. J (FLAT 3)’. Underneath, in another hand: ‘It’s sealed, relax!’",
 "evidence:evidence.owen_flour.name": "Hart Fuel stock",
 "evidence:evidence.owen_flour.summary": "In the cupboard under the stairs: 15 kg of peanut flour, one sack open.",
 "evidence:evidence.pen_tubes.detail": "Two empty carrier tubes on the rug, where the paramedics dropped them. Each is printed ‘Adrenaline auto-injector 0.15 mg’ and ‘EXP 08/2022’.\n\nThe pharmacy labels have been peeled off, leaving rectangles of tacky glue. These pens expired eighteen months ago.",
 "evidence:evidence.pen_tubes.name": "Empty pen tubes",
 "evidence:evidence.pen_tubes.summary": "0.15 mg pens, eighteen months out of date, their labels peeled off.",
 "evidence:evidence.pharmacy_bag.detail": "In the kitchen drawer: a pharmacy bag and an empty box. The dispensing label reads ‘Mr J. PRYCE — Adrenaline auto-injector 0.3 mg × 2 — carry at all times’, dated 26 February 2024. The box is stamped ‘EXP 09/2025’.\n\nTen days before he died, Jonah collected two new adult pens.",
 "evidence:evidence.pharmacy_bag.name": "Pharmacy bag",
 "evidence:evidence.pharmacy_bag.summary": "Jonah collected two new adult pens on 26 February.",
 "evidence:evidence.police_summary.detail": "Metropolitan Police — summary disclosed to Ashworth & Kaur, solicitors for Ms P. Ratnam.\n\nThursday 7 March 2024\n20:31 — Deceased (Jonah PRYCE, 34) orders from Thambi, Dalston, by delivery app. Order note: ‘SEVERE PEANUT ALLERGY’.\n21:04 — Order delivered, contactless, to Flat 3, The Ropeworks, Hackney Wick.\n21:33 — 999 call from deceased: allergic reaction, ‘pens not working’.\n21:44 — Ambulance arrives. 21:45 — Police force the door. Deceased in cardiac arrest; two used adrenaline pens beside him, both out of date — believed to be his own.\n22:19 — Pronounced dead, Homerton Hospital.\n\nFriday 8 March — public analyst finds peanut protein in the curry (report attached). Ms RATNAM arrested on suspicion of gross negligence manslaughter, released under investigation. Thambi closed by the council pending inquiry.\n\nNo suspicious circumstances noted by attending officers; curry and phone retained, flat released to the fiancée, 8 March. Coroner informed; inquest opened and adjourned.\n\nWorking theory: contamination at Thambi during packing — e.g. a garnish or condiment containing peanut, sprinkled over the curry. Deceased’s own expired pens a contributing factor.",
 "evidence:evidence.police_summary.name": "Police summary",
 "evidence:evidence.police_summary.summary": "The Met’s account of Thursday night, and its working theory.",
 "evidence:evidence.receipts_draft.detail": "A script on Jonah’s laptop, last edited Tuesday 5 March, 23:40, scheduled for Monday 11 March, 09:00:\n\n‘RECEIPTS. For a year, restaurants have been asked for “collab fees” through my business inbox — five hundred, a thousand, two thousand pounds. The ones who said no got a visit from me. I didn’t know. I found out last week, and I’m sick about it.\n\nI’m not going to hide who did it. It was the person I trusted most with my name. Monday, nine o’clock: names, screenshots, everything. Then I’m going to the police.’\n\nA folder beside it holds 31 screenshots.",
 "evidence:evidence.receipts_draft.name": "Draft video: RECEIPTS",
 "evidence:evidence.receipts_draft.summary": "To post Monday 9 a.m.: restaurants were shaken down in his name.",
 "evidence:evidence.sachet_corner.detail": "Pushed under the kickboard of the kitchen island: a torn corner of a silver foil sachet. Printed on it, in green:\n\n‘…NUT PROTEIN · 300 mg’\n‘…L IMMUNOTHERAPY — open and mix into food’",
 "evidence:evidence.sachet_corner.name": "Torn foil corner",
 "evidence:evidence.sachet_corner.summary": "From a sachet of peanut protein: ‘300 mg … open and mix into food’.",
 "evidence:evidence.smart_lock_log.detail": "Flat 3 front door — lock history, Thursday 7 March (the door locks itself a minute after it closes):\n\n18:12 Unlocked — JONAH (keypad)\n18:13 Locked — auto\n20:24 Unlocked — inside handle\n20:25 Locked — auto\n21:04 Unlocked — inside handle\n21:05 Locked — auto\n21:19 Unlocked — GUEST (keypad)\n21:20 Locked — auto\n21:24 Unlocked — inside handle\n21:25 Locked — auto\n21:45 Door forced — alarm\n\nCodes: JONAH · LENA · CLEANER (Mon & Thu, 09:00–12:00 only) · GUEST (‘family & team’)",
 "evidence:evidence.smart_lock_log.name": "Smart lock history",
 "evidence:evidence.smart_lock_log.summary": "21:19: Flat 3 opened with the guest code. 21:24: opened from inside, and locked again.",
 "evidence:evidence.thambi_bag.detail": "The paper bag Jonah’s order came in, on the island. It has been torn open down one side, the way Jonah does it in his 21:29 story. The round orange Thambi sticker is still on the fold at the top — but it is creased across the middle, one edge sits crooked over a small tear in the paper, and torn paper fibres are stuck to its underside.\n\nSomebody peeled it off and pressed it back on.",
 "evidence:evidence.thambi_bag.name": "The Thambi bag",
 "evidence:evidence.thambi_bag.summary": "Jonah tore it open down the side. Someone else had peeled the seal and pressed it back on.",
 "evidence:evidence.thambi_cctv.detail": "Thambi’s kitchen camera, Thursday 7 March:\n\n20:41 — Priya ladles chicken curry into a tub from the stock pot that fed three other customers that night, and snaps the lid on. No garnish, nothing sprinkled. None of the other customers reported a problem.\n20:47 — She packs order #4471, folds the bag and seals it with a round orange Thambi sticker.\n\nFrom 20:30 to 22:10 Priya never leaves the pass.",
 "evidence:evidence.thambi_cctv.name": "Thambi’s kitchen camera",
 "evidence:evidence.thambi_cctv.summary": "20:47: Priya seals the bag. From 20:30 to 22:10 she never leaves the pass.",
 "evidence:evidence.tutoring_log.detail": "Hannah’s account on the tutoring site, session history:\n\nThursday 7 March, 21:00–21:45 — Year 6 maths (fractions) with Kofi A. Video on throughout. Recording kept for 30 days.\n\nKofi’s mother has left a review: ‘Mrs Doyle was brilliant as always, even with her daughter shouting through the door at the end! ★★★★★’",
 "evidence:evidence.tutoring_log.name": "Hannah’s tutoring record",
 "evidence:evidence.tutoring_log.summary": "Thursday 21:00–21:45: maths with a Year 6 pupil, camera on throughout.",
 "suspects:suspects.hannah.bio": "Jonah’s older sister, a primary-school teacher who tutors online in the evenings, and the wife of his manager, Marcus. She has been on compassionate leave since Friday.",
 "suspects:suspects.hannah.dismissal": "I’m sorry — I don’t see what that has to do with anything.",
 "suspects:suspects.hannah.name": "Hannah Doyle",
 "suspects:suspects.hannah.rebuttal": "I was teaching a ten-year-old fractions, on camera, from nine until quarter to ten. I spent my whole life keeping peanuts away from my brother.",
 "suspects:suspects.hannah.role": "The sister",
 "suspects:suspects.lena.bio": "Jonah’s fiancée for a year and the editor of every video he posted. She was out at a pilates class, she says, and came home to find paramedics working on him. It was she who gave you the code to the flat.",
 "suspects:suspects.lena.dismissal": "No. That’s not what it means. You’re reading it wrong.",
 "suspects:suspects.lena.name": "Lena Novak",
 "suspects:suspects.lena.rebuttal": "Owen’s camera shows me in his flat the whole time. I was a coward and a cheat that night. I wasn’t a murderer.",
 "suspects:suspects.lena.role": "The fiancée",
 "suspects:suspects.marcus.bio": "Jonah’s manager at Doyle Talent, and his brother-in-law — he’s married to Jonah’s sister, Hannah. A former rower, six foot four, with a handshake like a vice. Jonah brought in most of the agency’s money.",
 "suspects:suspects.marcus.dismissal": "I negotiate for a living. You’re going to have to bring more than that.",
 "suspects:suspects.marcus.name": "Marcus Doyle",
 "suspects:suspects.marcus.rebuttal": "You’ve got a story, not a case. Jonah was family. Come back when you can prove it.",
 "suspects:suspects.marcus.role": "The manager",
 "suspects:suspects.mihai.bio": "The delivery rider who left Jonah’s curry at his door at 21:04, and the last person known to have handled the bag. The police want to speak to him again. He has not been easy to find.",
 "suspects:suspects.mihai.dismissal": "I don’t understand. I just bring the food.",
 "suspects:suspects.mihai.name": "Mihai Lungu",
 "suspects:suspects.mihai.rebuttal": "I put the bag down and I took the photo. You can see the sticker. Then I went to Bow with two pizzas. That is all.",
 "suspects:suspects.mihai.role": "The courier",
 "suspects:suspects.owen.bio": "A personal trainer who lives in Flat 1, downstairs from Jonah, and sells his own peanut protein balls online. Jonah once reviewed them in a video. He said they tasted like a gym bag.",
 "suspects:suspects.owen.dismissal": "Mate, I’ve no idea what you’re on about.",
 "suspects:suspects.owen.name": "Owen Hart",
 "suspects:suspects.owen.rebuttal": "My camera shows Lena in my flat, and me not leaving it. Hate the guy’s reviews, sure. I didn’t kill him.",
 "suspects:suspects.owen.role": "The neighbour",
 "suspects:suspects.priya.bio": "Chef-owner of Thambi, a nine-year-old Sri Lankan restaurant in Dalston, and your client. Jonah’s one-star review in January halved her bookings. Now she has been arrested, her restaurant is shut, and strangers send her death threats.",
 "suspects:suspects.priya.dismissal": "I’ve had food inspectors tougher than you. That proves nothing.",
 "suspects:suspects.priya.name": "Priya Ratnam",
 "suspects:suspects.priya.rebuttal": "I was at my pass all night — my own camera shows it. I fed that man because I wanted him to be wrong about me. I didn’t want him dead.",
 "suspects:suspects.priya.role": "The chef"
}
